Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?Mythic:=20ntdll=20ARM64EC=20=E2=80=94=20NULL-gu?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ard=20the=20KiUserExceptionDispatcher=20fast=20path?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

In a child pseudo-process's private ntdll copy the
__os_arm64x_dispatch_call_no_redirect slot can still be NULL
(per-process ntdll global not populated; the dispatcher re-patch is
skipped for ntdll itself). The naked-asm KiUserExceptionDispatcher then
did `blr x16` with x16=0 → jump to NULL → SEGV loop → dead thread —
observed killing steam.exe's relaunched bootstrapper on every guest
exception. The blr path is only a stack-cleanliness optimization, so a
NULL slot now falls through to the full dispatch_exception path.

Likely also fixes the taskmgr boot death (task #26, guest RIP=0 loop).

(cherry picked from commit d3e7c6165176e0aaecee4af73fe173e8bc74d628)
Madeira-commit: 2d0eccb169f708a091e728164a77f6bb53b7bd9d
Rebased: clean
Class: madeira-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-26-wine-latest-rebase.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c b/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c
index e945d25..c039587 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c
@@ -1599,6 +1599,14 @@ void __attribute__((naked)) KiUserExceptionDispatcher( EXCEPTION_RECORD *rec, CO
          /* bypass exit thunk to avoid messing up the stack */
          "adrp x16, __os_arm64x_dispatch_call_no_redirect\n\t"
          "ldr x16, [x16, #:lo12:__os_arm64x_dispatch_call_no_redirect]\n\t"
+         /* iOS-Mythic (task#29): in a child pseudo-process's private ntdll copy
+          * this slot is sometimes still NULL (per-process ntdll global not
+          * populated; arm64ec_process_init_dispatchers SKIPs ntdll re-patch).
+          * A NULL x16 here → `blr x16` to 0 → SEGV loop → dead thread (observed
+          * killing steam.exe). The `blr x16` path is only a stack-cleanliness
+          * optimization; label 1 (dispatch_exception) is the full, correct
+          * ARM64EC SEH dispatcher. So if the slot is NULL, fall through to it. */
+         "cbz x16, 1f\n\t"
          "mov x9, x0\n\t"
          "blr x16\n"
          "1:\tadd x0, sp, #0x3b0+0x4d0\n\t" /* rec */
